Job Description 
 Build the Future With Us 
 Are you passionate about accounting and enjoy contributing to the quality of financial information? As an Accounting Technician , you will play a key role in processing and monitoring financial transactions while contributing to the preparation of reliable financial statements and helping the organization achieve its objectives.
 This position is an excellent opportunity to put your accounting expertise to work in a collaborative environment where talent development, continuous improvement, and innovation are valued.
 What You’ll Accomplish With Us 
 As an Accounting Technician , you will be at the heart of our mission. Your main responsibilities will include:
 Record various transactions in the accounting system;
 Prepare month-end accounting entries and contribute to the preparation of financial statements;
 Perform various tasks related to cash processing;
 Issue cheques;
 Respond to requests and support various departments across the organization;
 Reconcile certain general ledger accounts;
 Assist in preparing information for internal and external auditors;
 Perform any other related duties required to support the smooth operation of the department.
 What Could Accelerate Your Success in This Role 
 We are looking for someone who:
 Holds a college diploma (DEC) in Business Administration, with a specialization in Accounting;
 Has 3 to 5 years of relevant accounting experience;
 Demonstrates a high level of accuracy and excellent attention to detail;
 Stands out for their ability to effectively manage priorities and meet deadlines;
 Is recognized for their teamwork and communication skills;
 Demonstrates autonomy, resourcefulness, and initiative;
 Is proficient with Microsoft Office, particularly Excel;
 Has any other combination of education and experience deemed relevant;
 Has a beginner level of English proficiency, as the incumbent will be required to respond to English-speaking internal teams and suppliers on a regular basis.
 Why You’ll Love Working With Us 
 An environment where collaboration, respect, and mutual support are valued;
 Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning;
 An inclusive workplace that encourages everyone to reach their full potential;
 A work environment focused on innovation and continuous improvement;
 Competitive benefits and an attractive total compensation package.
 Apply now and take charge of your career, where your talent truly matters! 
 Hesitating to Apply? 
 At iA, we believe in potential and value diverse experiences. If this role inspires you, take the leap and apply: your place may be with us, and we want to get to know you!
 Location(s) 
Quebec / 1080, Grande Allee West 
 Other Possible Location(s) 
 Company 
Industrial Alliance, Auto and Home Insurance Inc. 
 Posting End Date 
2026-11-23 
 Company Overview 
 iA Financial Group* is the strength of a company with a human side, with its over 8,000 employees. Together, we have earned the trust of our more than four million clients and 25,000 advisors who have chosen us for their insurance, savings, and wealth management.
 With over $200 billion in assets and half a billion invested in technological innovation, we’re a key player in the financial services industry in Canada and the United States. The secret to our success? Investing in you, one person at a time. Because, for over 125 years, we have believed that it’s by supporting our employees and surrounding ourselves with the most reputable leaders in the industry, we will continue to innovate.
 At iA, we’re invested in you.
 * iA Financial group includes of the following entities: iA Services financiers, iA assurance auto et habitation, iA Gestion privée de patrimoine, PPI Management, Investia, iA Gestion de placements, Prysm, iA Clarington, Michel Rhéaume et associés, Garanties Nationales, WGI Manufacturing, WGI Service Plan Division, Lubrico, iA Financement auto  
 Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion 
 At iA Financial Group, we support and celebrate diversity. We strive to provide a workplace that is recognized as inclusive for all, regardless of ethnic origin, nationality, language, religious beliefs, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, family situation, or physical or mental disability. 
 Please note that if you need help or assistance to make the recruitment process more accessible for you, please Contact us here . Someone from our team will be happy to assist you with your needs.
 Technology and Artificial Intelligence in Recruitment 
 To optimize and support our recruitment process, iA Financial Group may use certain technological tools, including artificial intelligence. These tools support the work of our recruiters but do not replace their judgment. All hiring decisions continue to be made by authorized individuals within the organization. For more information, please refer to our Privacy Notice .

