 About Krafton Montreal 
 We are a leading game development studio composed of veterans of the game industry. We are working on a game based on an acclaimed intellectual property set in an enthralling medieval fantasy world. 
 At Krafton Montreal, we believe in having fun while creating memorable experiences, being proud of our work, and showing respect for each other's contributions. 
 Job Description 
 As a Level Designer, you will design and deliver gameplay spaces and activities in our open world, for a third-person fantasy action game. You will turn game mechanics into engaging, readable and memorable experiences, with a constant focus on quality and iteration. 
 Working in Unreal Engine 5, you will collaborate closely with the design, art and development teams to create large-scale combat experiences. You will give each space its own pacing and identity, while clearly guiding the player through the action. 
 Responsibilities 
 Lead the design and development of levels, features and activity types, from concept through final implementation; 
 Design spaces suited to large-scale combat, with mastery of layout, arena pacing, enemy placement and contrast between spaces; 
 Create readable, varied combat experiences that guide player movement and support pacing, difficulty and key moments; 
 Quickly prototype different approaches, test them early and evolve them based on playtests and feedback, even if it means rethinking or completely rebuilding a space; 
 Adapt flexibly to production changes and take an experimental approach to keep combat experiences fresh; 
 Collaborate with artists, technical designers and programmers to align gameplay intent, constraints and solutions; 
 Clearly communicate design needs, risks and decisions to teams and directors; 
 Use scripting tools such as Blueprints to orchestrate events, sequences and key moments; 
 Contribute to the evolution of design guidelines, metrics and ways of working; 
 Mentor and support fellow level designers; 
 Take part in planning, scoping and prioritization of design work. 
 Knowledge & Skills 
 Solid professional experience in level design, with one or more shipped titles or equivalent production experience; 
 Excellent command of level design fundamentals, including layout, flow, pacing, readability and player guidance; 
 Experience designing combat spaces, ideally for large-scale battles or complex encounters; 
 Ability to structure the pacing of a fight through arena sequencing, enemy placement and contrast between spaces; 
 Ability to prototype and iterate quickly, test different ideas and incorporate feedback with an open mind; 
 Flexible, experimental mindset, able to adapt to change and challenge an approach when needed; 
 Excellent communication skills and a collaborative approach within cross-disciplinary teams, with the ability to present and defend design intent to leadership; 
 Hands-on experience with Unreal Engine 5; Blueprints proficiency is a significant asset; 
 Fluent in French (our primary working language) and comfortable working in English (used to communicate with our Korean headquarters); 
 Portfolio demonstrating strong level design skills and clear design intent (playable content is strongly recommended); 
